// Periodic apt configuration for unattended-upgrades, managed by the `common`
// role (spec task 3.1). This is the standard 20auto-upgrades enablement: refresh
// package lists daily and run the unattended-upgrade step. It schedules apt work
// only — no kernel/sysctl changes — so it is safe in an unprivileged LXC.
//
// SECRET-FREE: contains no secret material (requirement 1.5 / P3).
